      "content": "Somalia condemns deadly attack on church in Jordan | Horseed Media Skip to content Search Home Somalia News Puntland News World News in English Featured More.. Dowladda Federaalka Galmudug Hiiraan News Jubaland News Koonfur Galbeed SSC Somaliland Follow us Search News Somalia Somalia condemns deadly attack on church in Jordan Posted by: Horseed Staff Somalia has condemned a deadly attack on a Greek Orthodox church in Jordan’s Karak governorate, expressing solidarity with the Jordanian government and the families of those killed. 24 October, 2026 Share Tweet Eight people were killed and dozens wounded after gunmen opened fire on Friday during a funeral at a church in Hmoud village, about 90km (56 miles) south of the capital, Amman, according to Jordanian authorities. The death toll rose from seven to eight on Saturday after one of those critically injured died in hospital. “The Federal Republic of Somalia strongly condemns the terrorist attack in Karak Governorate, in the brotherly Hashemite Kingdom of Jordan, which killed and injured innocent people,” Somalia’s Foreign Ministry said in a statement. “Somalia knows the human cost of terrorism and rejects violence and extremism in all their forms,” the ministry added. Somalia extended its condolences to the families of those killed and wished those injured a speedy recovery. Jordanian authorities have described the shooting as a terrorist attack. Health officials said at least 40 people were wounded, with dozens still receiving treatment on Saturday. Jordan declared three days of national mourning following the attack, with flags ordered to half-staff at government institutions. Authorities have not publicly identified the attackers or announced a motive. Security forces continued efforts to identify and arrest those responsible. King Abdullah II condemned the attack and said those responsible would face justice, while Prime Minister Jafar Hassan described the shooting as an assault on all Jordanians. The attack has drawn condemnation from governments and international organisations across the region and beyond, as authorities continue their investigation into the circumstances and motive behind the shooting. Explore more on these topics Jordan Somalia Related Posts Somalia pledges support for Ugandan businesses as trade ties deepen 3 min read Somali Prime Minister Hamza Abdi Barre arrives in Jeddah 1 min read Somalia: Ali Gudlawe Hussein re-elected as Hirshabelle leader 1 min read Somaliland journalist detained after interviewing Somalia presidential hopeful 2 min read Back to top Horseed Media About Profile Contact us Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Category Wararka Soomaaliya Puntland News News Somalia Dowladda Federaalka World News ©2026 Horseed Media Ltd",
      "summary": "Somalia has condemned a deadly attack on a Greek Orthodox church in Jordan's Karak governorate, expressing solidarity with the Jordanian government and the victims' families. The attack occurred during a funeral in Hmoud village, resulting in eight fatalities and numerous injuries, with the death toll rising after one critically injured victim succumbed to their wounds. Somalia's Foreign Ministry issued a statement denouncing the terrorist act, emphasizing the country’s understanding of the human cost of terrorism and its rejection of violence and extremism. The attack has prompted Jordan to declare three days of national mourning, with flags at government institutions flown at half-staff. Jordanian authorities have labeled the shooting a terrorist attack, with ongoing efforts to identify and apprehend the perpetrators. King Abdullah II and Prime Minister Jafar Hassan condemned the violence, asserting that it is an affront to all Jordanians. The incident has garnered widespread condemnation from various governments and international organizations as investigations continue.",
